story:
Bad characters in query causes 500 response; expecting 400?

If I make the following call:

https://api.usergrid.com/org/app/collection?ql=where%20thirdPropertyTypeInt%20%3E%2030000%20&&%20thirdPropertyTypeInt%20%3C%2040000&limit=10

I get the response:

{code}
{
  "error": "null_pointer",
  "timestamp": 1435176848310,
  "duration": 1,
  "exception": "java.lang.NullPointerException"
}
{code}

The cause is that the ampersands in the query string aren't url encoded (should be %26 instead of &). I would expect that if the query string is bad, we should be returning a 400 Bad Request, rather than an ominous NullPointerException/500.
